\newlabel{tab:inference}{{3}{11}{MTEB split-11 paired effects at $k=8$. $\Delta $ RMSE is trace-risk minus comparator, so negative favors trace-risk. Intervals are marginal 95\% component-block percentile intervals conditional on fixed fits. Tests use paired component MSE differences; their $p$-values need not agree with bootstrap RMSE-interval exclusions. Holm covers eight comparisons. With six components no corrected rejection is attainable}{table.caption.8}{}}
\newlabel{tab:inference@cref}{{[table][3][]3}{[1][11][]11}{}{}{}}
\newlabel{tab:common}{{4}{11}{Pair-specific common-unseen RMSE on MTEB split 11 at $k=8$ (lower is better). Only tasks queried by neither policy are scored. Shared-task counts and MSEs are averaged over random paths where applicable before taking square roots. Intersections differ by comparator, so rows cannot be treated as one common-target leaderboard}{table.caption.9}{}}
\newlabel{tab:common@cref}{{[table][4][]4}{[1][11][]11}{}{}{}}
\newlabel{tab:perseed}{{5}{12}{MTEB full-suite group-macro RMSE for every split at the fixed budget $k=8$. Seeds overlap in model/component membership and are not independent test samples}{table.caption.10}{}}
\newlabel{tab:perseed@cref}{{[table][5][]5}{[1][11][]12}{}{}{}}
\newlabel{tab:splits}{{6}{12}{Split sizes and validation-selected hyperparameters. $M$ counts rows actually used and $G$ counts represented components; MTEB validation/test contain complete anchors only. Training includes eligible incomplete rows, so these counts do not partition all 278 rows. Seven of the 40 MTEB training components contain complete anchors. OpenLLM component sizes and split row counts remain imbalanced after repair; this table makes no causal attribution for that imbalance. Shrinkage $\alpha $, factor rank, and ridge are chosen before test scoring}{table.caption.11}{}}
\newlabel{tab:splits@cref}{{[table][6][]6}{[1][11][]12}{}{}{}}
\newlabel{tab:convergence}{{7}{13}{Gaussian stress convergence and support. Retention is the observed fraction among retained nonempty training rows, hence excludes empty rows; it is not guaranteed to equal the nominal retention probability. MCAR 20\% has two additional infeasible attempts omitted from the executable denominator. ``Max. change'' is the largest final stopping statistic; minimum pair support is an unweighted observed-row count. Complete/MCAR/MNAR use training anchors; diagonal/weak-shrinkage use natural histories}{table.caption.12}{}}
\newlabel{tab:convergence@cref}{{[table][7][]7}{[1][11][]13}{}{}{}}
\newlabel{tab:calibration}{{8}{13}{Descriptive Gaussian uncertainty diagnostics at the fixed comparison budgets, averaged over five overlapping splits. Model RMSE is $\sqrt {\tr C/p}$; actual RMSE is the held-out full-suite error. Coverage is the group-macro fraction of unseen entries inside nominal 90\% marginal Gaussian intervals. This is neither simultaneous coverage nor a validated post-selection guarantee}{table.caption.13}{}}
\newlabel{tab:calibration@cref}{{[table][8][]8}{[1][11][]13}{}{}{}}
\newlabel{tab:policytest}{{9}{13}{Test evaluation of the two validation-selected frozen OpenLLM $k=4$ policies after grouping repair (post-review exploratory reanalysis). Brackets are marginal 95\% component-bootstrap intervals conditional on the fitted policy, not simultaneous selection-adjusted adequacy bounds. No MTEB policy is selected. The unseen intervals are deterministic rescalings of the full-suite intervals}{table.caption.14}{}}
\newlabel{tab:policytest@cref}{{[table][9][]9}{[1][11][]13}{}{}{}}
\newlabel{tab:adequacy}{{10}{13}{Validation adequacy decisions and held-out point errors at the selected budgets. \textbf {The final column is post-hoc test-curve description only}: it is not validation, not the frozen deployed policy, and not evidence to choose a budget. ``None'' means no evaluated $k<p$ qualifies, not that every possible policy fails. Tolerances are illustrative and fixed at 2 full-suite / 3 unseen score points}{table.caption.15}{}}
\newlabel{tab:adequacy@cref}{{[table][10][]10}{[1][11][]13}{}{}{}}
